1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Hsiao-kung Jên Huang-hou''' 孝恭仁皇后, 1660–1723, June 25, secondary consort of Emperor Shêng-tsu, and mother of his fourth son and successor (see under Yin-chên), was the daughter of Wei-wu 威武 (also written 衛武) of 
2 CONC the Uya 烏雅 clan, a lieutenant-colonel belonging to the Manchu Plain Yellow Banner. In 1679, the year following the birth of Yin-chên, she was made secondary consort of the fourth rank with the title of '''Tê-pin''' 德嬪, and in 1682
2 CONC  after the Emperor's sixth son, Yin-tso 胤祚 (1680–1685), was born to her, she was raised to the third rank with the title of '''Tê-fei''' 德妃. She was also the mother of his ninth daughter, later called Princess Wên-hsien 温憲公主 (1683
2 CONC –1702), wife of Sunggayan (see under T'ung Kuo-wei); of his fourteenth son, Yin-t'i [q.v.]; and of two of his short-lived daughters. When her son Yin-chên ascended the throne as Emperor Shih-tsung in 1723, she was made Empress Dow
2 CONC ager (皇太后) with the title '''Jên-shou''' 仁壽 but died in the same year, age sixty-four (''sui''). She was given posthumously the status of Empress with the title '''Hsiao-kung Jên Huang-hou''', and was buried at Ching Ling 景陵, the 
2 CONC tomb of Emperor Shêng-tsu.
2 CONT
2 CONT [1/220/9b; 1/173/5b; ''Ch'ing lieh-ch'ao Hou-fei chuan-kao'' (see under Su-shun) shang 89b; ''Ch'ing Huang-shih ssŭ-p'u'' (see under Fu-lung-an), 2/11b, 4/12b, 4/13b, 3/13b, 3/15b.]
2 CONT
