1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kashyapa (IAST: Kaśyapa) is a revered Vedic sage of Hinduism.[1] He is one of the Saptarishis, the seven ancient sages of the Rigveda,[note 1] numerous Sanskrit texts and Indian mythologies.[4][5] He is the most an
2 CONC cient rishi listed in the colophon verse in the Brihadaranyaka Upanishad.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT * Parents	 Marichi (father)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ka%C5%9Bjapa
2 CONT
2 CONT Wives and children[edit] The Puranas and the Epics of Indian tradition mention Kashyapa and his genealogy numerous times. These are inconsistent, with allegorical stories exalting him as the father of all gods, men, demons and emp
2 CONC irical universe, in some conflated as the Kurma avatar of the Hindu god Vishnu.[37] In the Vishnu Purana, Kashyapa marries thirteen daughters of Daksha: Aditi, Diti, Kadru, Danu, Arishta, Surasa, Surabhi, Vinata, Tamra, Krodhavash
2 CONC a, Ira, Vishva and Muni.[5][38][39]
2 CONT
2 CONT Kashyapa, in the Vishnu Purana and Vayu Purana, is attributed to be the father of the Devas, Asuras, Yakshas, Dravidas and all living creatures with various daughters of Daksha. He married Aditi, with whom he fathered Surya or alt
2 CONC ernatively Agni, the Adityas, and in two inconsistent versions Vamana, an avatar of Vishnu, is the child of Aditi and Kashyapa.[40] In these fables, Kashyapa is the brother-in-law of Dharma and Adharma, both of whom are also descr
2 CONC ibed as married to other daughters of Daksha.[41] 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kashyapa
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of the Devas, Asuras, Nagas and all ofhumanity. He married Aditi, with whom he fathered Agni, theAdityas, and most importantly Lord Vishnu took his fifth Avataras Vamana, the son of Aditi, in the seventh Manvanta
2 CONC ra.[2]With his second wife, Diti, he begot the Daityas. Diti and Aditi were daughters of King Daksha Prajapati and sisters to Sati,Shiva's consort. Kashyap received the earth, obtained byParashurama's conquest of King Kartavirya A
2 CONC rjuna and henceforth, earth came to be known as "Kashyapi".
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also the author of the treatise Kashyap Samhita, orBraddha Jivakiya Tantra, which is considered, a classical reference book on Ayurveda especially in the fields of Ayurvedic pediatrics, gynecology and obstetrics.[3] It can 
2 CONC be safely assumed that there were many Kashyaps and the name indicates a status and not just one individual.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kashyapa ________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Kashyap (Sanskrit कश्यपkaśyap) was an ancient sage (rishis), who is one of theSaptarshis in the presentManvantara; with others beingAtri, Vashishtha, Vishvamitra,Gautama, Jamadagni,Bharadwaja [1] He was the father of the Devas,As
2 CONC uras, Nagas and all ofhumanity. He married Aditi, with whom he fathered Agni, theAdityas, and most importantly Lord Vishnu took his fifth avtaras Vamana, the son of Aditi, in the seventh Manvantara [2]. With his second wife, Diti,
2 CONC  he begot the Daityas. Diti and Aditi were daughters of King DakshaPrajapati and sisters to Sati,Shiva's consort. Kashyap received the earth, obtained byParashurama's conquest of KingKartavirya Arjuna and henceforth, earth came to
2 CONC  be known as "Kashyapi". He was also the author of the treatise Kashyap Samhita, orBraddha Jivakiya Tantra, which is considered, a classical reference book on Ayurvedaespecially in the fields of Ayurvedic pediatrics, gynecology an
2 CONC d obstetrics.[3] It can be safely assumed that there were many Kashyaps and the name indicates a status and not just one individual. Birth and Lineage of Kashyapa He is the son of Marichi, one of the ten sons (Maanasa-putras) of t
2 CONC he Creator Brahma. ThePrajapati Daksha gave his thirteen daughters (Aditi, Diti,Kadru, Danu, Arishta, Surasa,Surabhi, Vinata, Tamra,Krodhavaśā, Ida, Khasa andMuni [4] in marriage to Kashyapa.
