1 TITL Prajāpati
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}                    
2 CONT  Daksha Prajapati and his Descendants Daksha Prajapati was born out of the right thumb of Brahma and all the people were his descendants. He had one thousand sons and fifty daughters. He married thirteen of his daughters to Rishi 
2 CONC Kashyap. Kashyap, by his first wife had sons like Indra and Vivaswan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When Vivaswan got married, he had two sons-- Manu, the father of mankind and Yamraj, the god of death. All the dynasties on the earth descended from Manu's sons. Brahmins, Kshatriyas, Vaisyas and Shudras, were his descendents. Man
2 CONC u had ten sons --- Ven, Dhrishnu, Narishyant, Naabhag, Ikshwaku, Kaarush, Sharyati, Ila Kanya, Prishadhra and Nabhagarishti. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ila Kanya had a son called Pururava. She was both the father and the mother of Pururava. Pururava became the ruler of thirteen islands and even though he was a human being he indulged in hedonistic and animalistic pleasures. Intox
2 CONC icated with his power and strength he looted the brahmins and took away their wealth. The sages became angry with him and their curses destroyed him. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pururava had six sons by Urvashi whom he had brought from heaven. They were called Aayu, Dheeman, Amavasu, Dridhayu, Vanayu and Shatayu. Aayu's wife was called Swarbhanavi. She had five sons --- Nahush, Vridhasharma, Raji, Gaya an
2 CONC d Anena. Aayu's eldest son Nahush was a great scholar and a very brave king. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He ruled his kingdom according to the Dharma. Once due to his immense arrogance he made the seven celestial saints, the Saptrishi, carry him in a palanquin. He insulted them and that ultimately became the cause of his downfall. He
2 CONC  had six sons --- Yati, Yayati, Sanyati, Aayaati, Ayati and Dhruva. Yati became an ascetic and Yayati became the king.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Story of Daksha Prajapati Daksha Prajapati was born out of the right thumb of Brahma and all the people were his descendants. He had one thousand sons and fifty daughters. He married thirteen of his daughters to Rishi Kashyap. Kas
2 CONC hyap, by his first wife had sons like Indra and Vivaswan.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Vivaswan got married, he had two sons Manu, the father of mankind and Yamraj, the god of death. All the dynasties on the earth descended from Manu's sons. Brahmins, Kshatriyas, Vaisyas and Shudras, were his descendents. Manu 
2 CONC had ten sons Ven, Dhrishnu, Narishyant, Naabhag, Ikshwaku, Kaarush, Sharyati, Ila Kanya, Prishadhra and Nabhagarishti.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ila Kanya had a son called Pururava. She was both the father and the mother of Pururava. Pururava became the ruler of thirteen islands and even though he was a human being he indulged in hedonistic and animalistic pleasures. Intox
2 CONC icated with his power and strength he looted the brahmins and took away their wealth. The sages became angry with him and their curses destroyed him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pururava had six sons by Urvashi whom he had brought from heaven. They were called Aayu, Dheeman, Amavasu, Dridhayu, Vanayu and Shatayu. Aayu's wife was called Swarbhanavi. She had five sons Nahush, Vridhasharma, Raji, Gaya and An
2 CONC ena. Aayu's eldest son Nahush was a great scholar and a very brave king.
2 CONT
2 CONT He ruled his kingdom according to the Dharma. Once due to his immense arrogance he made the seven celestial saints, the Saptrishi, carry him in a palanquin. He insulted them and that ultimately became the cause of his downfall. He
2 CONC  had six sons Yati, Yayati, Sanyati, Aayaati, Ayati and Dhruva. Yati became an ascetic and Yayati became the king.
